    "narrative": "The LawDog starting lineup for 2026-05-11 is headlined by **Taylor Ward** (69.76) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53), both of whom benefit significantly from facing Sasaki. **Taylor Ward** earns the top spot on our board today, buoyed by a substantial +16% park factor adjustment and a favorable platoon edge against the left-handed Weathers, keeping him squarely in the elite tier for daily efficiency. **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02) are also high-confidence starts; the matchup against Sasaki\u2019s 5.30 xERA allows both to maximize their plate appearance frequency and contact rates, with **Jung Hoo Lee** seeing a massive boost from his prime spot at the top of the order. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (69.49) remains an anchor for the team despite a tougher matchup against Suter, as his elite base floor consistently overrides the marginal SP skill concern.\n\nThe most challenging roster decision today involves balancing the middle infield and catcher slots. **Cal Raleigh** (57.36) edges out a crowded field of candidates, as his power profile remains our best bet for counting stats even against a respectable arm like Lambert. While **Will Smith** (45.82) is active, his matchup against McDonald\u2019s elite 2.60 xERA drags his efficiency score down toward our marginal threshold; however, we are starting him today to ensure we don't bleed games played while **Yainer Diaz** remains sidelined on the IL. We are currently navigating a light day for our bench depth, with **Lawrence Butler**, **Tyler Freeman**, and **Bryson Stott** all unavailable due to scheduling, leaving no real pivot options should a late lineup scratch occur. \n\nStrategic risks are minimal today, but we are keeping a close watch on **Daulton Varsho** (56.23). While his raw score is bolstered by a +10% platoon edge and the potential for a stolen base given the slow delivery of Rasmussen, the opposing SP skill (-8%) is the primary drag on his profile. We are leaning into his utility today specifically to target the scarcity of stolen bases, as our algorithm prioritizes his sprint-related upside despite the tough pitching environment. As always, we are monitoring all lineups closely for any shifts in order that would diminish the projected value for **Brendan Donovan** or **Geraldo Perdomo**, both of whom are currently providing necessary efficiency from the top-to-middle third of their respective orders.",
